  "visualDNA": {
    "Overview": "Traditionally, the Yomut carpet uses gul motifs in different shapes and sizes. Commonly edged with florets, the Yomut carpet is noted by Britannica for its borders that usually follow a geometric vine design. Diamond-shaped motifs, attached by latch hooks, are also a common observation in the carpet. Britannica described its color pallet as ranging from a reddish brown to plum shades."
